# Canonical Turtle for the protocol-derived encoding of:
#   E. Slootman et al. (2024). Accurate Quantum Monte Carlo Forces for Machine-Learned Force Fields: Ethanol as a Benchmark.
#   Journal of Chemical Theory and Computation. doi:10.1021/acs.jctc.4c00498  arXiv:2404.09755v1
#
# Version read: arxiv-preprint arXiv:2404.09755v1 (sha256 8f52e4cd5b39ca0d...);
#   the DOI above is cited, numbers are those of the version read.
# Corpus rank 609 (Dataset/benchmark). Method identity follows
#   artifacts/kg/METHODS.md (registry: artifacts/kg/methods-registry.csv).
# Generated by artifacts/scripts/encode_paper.py from artifacts/kg/encoding/specs/slootman2024.yaml.
#
# Encoding scope: the eight sGDML models of ethanol trained on the 200
# configurations of set A (100 train, 100 validation) with forces from
# VMC, DMC (reweighting, RE-hybrid, variational-drift) with one-determinant
# Jastrow-Slater wave functions, PBE-TS, PBE0-MBD and CCSD(T) with cc-pVTZ
# and cc-pVQZ, with their force MADs against CCSD(T) (Table II) on set A
# (cc-pVQZ reference) and on the independent set C (cc-pVTZ reference).
# The reference-method force errors (Table I) compare electronic-structure
# methods, not MLIPs.

@prefix rdf: <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .
@prefix schema: <https://schema.org/> .
@prefix mls: <http://www.w3.org/ns/mls#> .
@prefix unit: <http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/> .
@prefix mlips: <https://w3id.org/mlips#> .
@prefix entity: <https://w3id.org/mlips/entity/> .

###############################################################################
# Q1 -- Bibliographic identification
###############################################################################

entity:study-slootman2024 a mlips:BenchmarkStudy ;
    rdfs:label "Slootman et al. (2024): quantum Monte Carlo forces as reference data for machine-learned force fields, ethanol benchmark" ;
    mlips:reportedIn entity:article-slootman2024 .

entity:article-slootman2024 a schema:ScholarlyArticle ;
    schema:sameAs <https://doi.org/10.1021/acs.jctc.4c00498> ;
    schema:datePublished "2024"^^xsd:gYear ;
    schema:name "Accurate Quantum Monte Carlo Forces for Machine-Learned Force Fields: Ethanol as a Benchmark" ;
